WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:04.529
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie Hail Hydra.

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:08.890
So This week’s Agents of SHIELD was a direct
continuation of the end of Winter Soldier.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:12.990
In terms of pacing it really is the start
of the final plot arc of season 1.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:19.369
What I’m going to do first is talk about
how the movie and the tv show connected, then

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:21.210
top 5 moments, then my review.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:27.159
During that part I’ll also address what
all the shit hitting the fan means for season

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:31.560
2 if the show gets renewed.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.640
Also heads up, my bonus Marvel video this
week will be a Captain America 3 video.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.230
I think I’ve figured out which comics they’re
going to be using for it.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.590
Be sure to subscribe to get it if you’re
finding me for the first time.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:47.710
So let’s talk about Winter Soldier crossing
into Agents of SHIELD.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.280
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the movie or this episode.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.750
The timeline is like this, they HYDRA helicarrier
strike started right before this episode started.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.300
The end of Winter Soldier, when Captain America
destroys them, happens just as they are capturing

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.300
Agent Garrett and his men.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.300
They’re at the Triskelion.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.300
Remember they parked the Bus in the same hanger
we saw in the movie.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.790
When Victoria Hand said Captain America’s
whereabouts are unknown, that’s around the

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.900
time he was at Nick Fury’s grave with Anthony
Mackie.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.370
Nick Fury still wants everyone to think he’s
dead.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.020
So Coulson and Hand still don’t know he
survived.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.560
He’s off trying to track down more rogue
HYDRA agents.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:22.190
Captain America and Anthony Mackie are doing
the same thing separately while they hunt

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:23.940
for the Winter Soldier.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.380
So this episode ended pretty much at the same
time the Winter Soldier movie ended.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.840
Obviously the show has 5 more episodes.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.570
But we can talk about where it’s headed
after my top 5 moments.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.570
And they are:

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.670
Number 5 - Skye Decodes The HYDRA activation
message

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:42.700
The message was sent to all the HYDRA double
agents telling them to sieze control of SHIELD.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.880
That went out while they were launching the
Helicarriers in the movie.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.090
When Crossbones and Robert Redford revealed
who they really were.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.210
I love the reaction of Coulson and the crew.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:59.229
Since I saw the movie last week, the surprise
wasn’t as wasted, but I loved those lines.

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:01.310
Out of the shadows and into the light.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.180
Time to face the Hydra Music.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.850
Which makes me wonder, what does the Hydra
theme music sound like?

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.030
Maybe like the Star Wars Imperial March.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.819
Number 4 - May Comes Clean About TAHITI

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:17.040
Before this, there were two people I thought
she could be reporting to based on her alliegance.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.160
Robert Redford and Nick Fury.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.180
I’m glad she turned out to not be a double
agent for HYDRA.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.000
How cool was it that she basically inceptioned
their whole team into Coulson’s head via

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Fury.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.750
Like she gave Fury all their names and Fury
suggested them to Coulson.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.870
I’m curious to see what her relationship
with him will be like once they dust settles.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:42.370
I’m expecting some game changing May save
in the finale that makes him start trusting

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.370
her again.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.439
But for the next couple of episodes she’ll
just be an ally.

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:46.439
Not a friend.

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:49.849
Number 3 - Victoria Hand’s HYDRA Fakeout

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:52.590
One of the many awesome fakeouts in the episode.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:56.420
When we saw that end teaser last week that
revealed she was remote piloting the plane

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.220
I was pretty sure she wasn’t the clairvoyant.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.430
So when she gave them the HYDRA speech I was
actually surprised.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:07.800
In the comics Victoria Hand works for HAMMER,
but she isn’t outright evil like HYDRA.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.040
When she took it all back and said they passed
the test I was relieved.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.879
Had she been an actual HYDRA agent, they probably
would have had to eventually kill her off

00:03:15.879 --> 00:03:19.760
the show unless she was going to go on to
become some new big bad.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.300
And nothing I saw gave me the impression that
she was going to be a season 2 big bad.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.670
Number 2 - Garrett is the Clairvoyant

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.990
Surprisingly not the biggest reveal in the
episode.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:36.590
Bill Paxton does such an amazing job of playing
sleazebag characters, how could we not have

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.360
known he would turn out to be a sleazebag
double agent for HYDRA.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.290
To be fair, he wasn’t always HYDRA, he said
he saw the wind blowing in their direction

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.290
and switched sides.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:49.410
So I think when he and Coulson were training
together under Nick Fury he was still on the

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.410
good side.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:56.769
In the comics Garrett eventually became an
Avenger, but he was a pretty awful person

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.090
before all that happened.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.333
I’ll talk more about where I think his character
is headed in a sec.

00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:03.880
and my Number 1 WTF moment - Ward Is Hydra.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.380
Or Is He?

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:09.240
Huge reveal, Ward shoots Victoria Hand and
the guards so we’re supposed to think he’s

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.020
either HYDRA or just decided to turn right
there on the spot.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.670
But wait, let’s think about this for a sec.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.199
Personally I think he’s just playing Garrett
in order to uncover who the other top level

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:21.680
HYDRA agents are.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.250
Like Ward is a double double agent.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:25.690
So he’s still a good guy.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.000
What about the gun shots though?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.160
Did he really kill Victoria Hand?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.000
We didn’t see blood and remember Couslon
told them to use the night night guns when

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
they first landed at SHIELD headquarters.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.440
We never saw him switch guns, so he probably
was still using the stun gun and it only appeared

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.740
he was using real bullets.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:44.900
I don’t remember them ever telling Agent
Garrett about the Night Night Gun technology.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.660
That was something Fitz developed on his own.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.330
It’s not normal SHIELD technology.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.520
Thus I think either next week or in a couple
more episodes.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.610
We’ll find out Ward is secretly on a mission
and he’s not a HYDRA agent.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:05:02.889
So real quick here are just some bonus favorite
moments that I thought were really amazing.

00:05:02.889 --> 00:05:09.880
Garrett give Agents Stilwell a shout out for
hiring so many HYDRA agents.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:15.630
Garrett tries to recruit Fitz to be HYDRA’s
new Arnim Zola, May calls out Ward for having

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:20.669
a hard on for Skye and then Skye and Ward’s
let’s have a drink moment.

00:05:20.669 --> 00:05:24.780
They’re officially the second biggest ‘ship
on the show next to Coulson and the Cellist.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.860
We’re actually going to meet the cellist
pretty soon.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.200
She’s being played by Amy Acker.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.389
Now it’s your turn though, let me know what
your favorite moment was?

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:33.860
Was it all the fakeouts?

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:38.450
Learning Garrett was the true Clairvoyant
or the Ward reveal at the end?

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.310
Overall I rate the episode as a solid B plus.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:45.830
It did a good job of incorporating this huge
convoluted movie plot from Winter Soldier,

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.460
a two and a half hour movie.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.470
Not an easy job.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:52.210
And it revealed all these new layers in the
existing characters.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.910
I love what they’re doing with the relationships
on the team.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.949
Not just the sexual relationships, the friendships
like Coulson and May.

00:05:58.949 --> 00:06:02.639
I fully expect all the broken trust issues
to be fixed by the end.

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:08.759
But the HYDRA cat and mouse chase is going
to be so much fun to watch between now and

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:16.970
then.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:36.190
They slipped in 
a couple nice callbacks to Gravitonium, I

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:39.900
keep expecting Graviton to bust out of the
fridge with all this chaos happening.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:44.699
And I have to say I was honestly surprised
that the Clairvoyant wasn’t Arnim Zola,

00:06:44.699 --> 00:06:47.430
it was Garrett a real person all along.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.060
I was a little dissapointed.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:55.160
I really liked the idea of AI being evil given
the plot of Avengers 2.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.440
The only other thing I really didn’t like
about the episode was that scene where they’re

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.270
carting Garrett off and it’s in slow motion
with this weird music track.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.270
It just felt really odd.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:06.419
It would have been better if Triplett had
just rushed up and tackled him like the Hulk.

00:07:06.419 --> 00:07:15.039
Real Quick let’s talk about what SHIELD
crashing down says about Season 2 of the show.

00:07:15.039 --> 00:07:19.229
It hasn’t been renewed yet even though every
single other show on ABC has gotten a renewal

00:07:19.229 --> 00:07:20.389
or cancellation notice.

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:22.570
They haven’t said anything about SHIELD.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:25.850
I think it’s because they’re trying to
hide or at least hold off on revealing what’s

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.330
going to happen during the season finale.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:34.319
I’ll be talking more about this in my Bonus
Captain America 3 video tomorrow, because

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:35.419
it’s all about the Secret Avengers comic.

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:38.490
SHIELD gets destroyed and Captain America
puts together a separate team of his own to

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.770
go on covert missions.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:44.639
I think the show Agents of SHIELD will be
doing something like this in season 2 if it’s

00:07:44.639 --> 00:07:45.639
not cancelled.

00:07:45.639 --> 00:07:48.630
Like I said, I’ll explain more in the bonus
video tomorrow.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.470
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.260
Let me know what your final thoughts on the
episode were.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.670
Did you think the episode did a good job of
holding up the suspense from the movie?

00:07:55.670 --> 00:08:00.630
I saw the movie almost a week ago, I think
the episode would have seemed better if I’d

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.610
seen the movie right before seeing it.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:07.330
But it was still a lot of fun.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:10.050
Next week Patton Oswalt is guest starring,
so be sure to watch.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:14.070
In the meantime you can click here for that
bonus Captain America 3 Secret Avengers video.

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:16.180
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:20.500
And you can click here for my other picks
for a Captain America 3 story.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.400
Thanks for watching, Hail Hydra.

